{"name":"Tribal Pottery","hex":"#a78876","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tribal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to tribes.","Based on or organized according to tribes."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A design or image that has been influenced by indigenous peoples; especially such a tattoo.","A member of a tribe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribal"},{"term":"pottery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Fired ceramic wares that contain clay when formed.","A potter's shop or workshop, where pottery is made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pottery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tribe","blocks":[{"text":"The term tribe is used in many different contexts to refer to a category of human social group. The predominant worldwide use of the term in English is in the discipline of anthropology. The definition is contested, in part due to conflicting theoretical understandings of social and kinship structures, and also reflecting the problematic application of this concept to extremely diverse human societies. Its concept is often contrasted by anthropologists with other social and kinship groups, being hierarchically larger than a lineage or clan, but smaller than a chiefdom, ethnicity, nation or state. These terms are similarly disputed. In some cases, tribes have legal recognition and some degree of political autonomy from national or federal government, but this legalistic usage of the term may conflict with anthropological definitions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/War_on_the_Plains_Comanche_vs_Osage_by_George_Catlin_1834.png/330px-War_on_the_Plains_Comanche_vs_Osage_by_George_Catlin_1834.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribe","wikidata":"Q133311"},{"title":"Pottery","blocks":[{"text":"Pottery is the process and the products of forming vessels and other objects with clay and other raw materials, which are fired at high temperatures to give them a hard and durable form. The place where a potter makes such wares is also called a pottery. The definition of pottery, used by the ASTM International, is \"all fired ceramic wares that contain clay when formed, except technical, structural, and refractory products\". End applications include tableware, decorative ware, sanitary ware, and in technology and industry such as electrical insulators and laboratory ware. In art history and archaeology, especially of ancient and prehistoric periods, pottery often means only vessels, and sculpted figurines of the same material are called terracottas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Traditional_pottery_in_Nigeria_%28Ikpu_ite%29_19.jpg/330px-Traditional_pottery_in_Nigeria_%28Ikpu_ite%29_19.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pottery","wikidata":"Q11642"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png/500px-Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png/1280px-Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png/500px-Isolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of uncontacted tribes, around the start of the 21st century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIsolierte-V%C3%B6lker.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Table_Service_MET_DT11573_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Table_Service_MET_DT11573_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum